<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick I, Burgrave of Nuremberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1200</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Frederick III of Zollern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick I was a count of Zollern, as Frederick III, who became burgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> around 1192 through his marriage to Sophia of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raba">Raabs</a>, heiress of the previous burgraves. A loyal follower of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Staufer</a> emperors, he founded the Franconian line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a>: his sons divided his lands, one taking the Swabian county of Zollern and the other the burgraviate, whose descendants later ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p></div>
